node_modules/
dist/
.DS_Store
.claude/

# Run output — regenerated per session, not source (S94). The seven
# mica-*-witness-readback-*.txt files from S93 stay ON DISK and are ignored
# here rather than deleted; a re-lay must not carry them into /opt.
# NB the brief's literal pattern `mica-*-witness-readback-*.txt` matches only
# SIX of the seven: mica-mutation-demo-20260828-witness-readback.txt has no
# trailing segment after `readback`. Widened here; tested, not assumed.
mica-*witness-readback*.txt

# The relay's vintage claim (S106b). WRITTEN AT RELAY, INTO THE LAID TREE, and
# never committed: a VINTAGE file that rode a commit would be rsynced along with
# it and would then claim, from inside /opt, a hash that is not what was laid.
# A stale claim is worse than no claim — the banner's ABSENT branch is honest.
/VINTAGE

# Python bytecode from scripts/ (declare-*.py and their tests)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Phase-1 contradiction probe scratch (build seat, S139 Act B). Not source.
.actb-probe/

# The opens-sweep's captures (S185). The sweep writes its tsv rows under out/, and
# those rows are EVIDENCE for a receipt, not source. Until this line existed they
# were untracked-AND-unignored, which is precisely what the relay's step-0 clean
# check refuses — so the tool that produces the relay's evidence was the reason
# the relay could not run. Measured: 3 files, `git status` 5 lines, before this.
out/
